# Mutation cases for "a transition with no target ends a microstep, not the
# macrostep" on the engine that already answered it correctly.
#
# Run with
# `scripts/mutate sce-build/tests/mutations/targetless_transition_completes_macrostep_rust.cases`.
#
# The Kotlin generator's half is in
# `targetless_transition_completes_macrostep.cases` and the two C++ engines are
# in `targetless_transition_completes_macrostep_ctest.cases`. This file guards
# the side of the comparison that was right on first measurement.
#
# That is worth a round rather than a note. This engine is correct because
# `run_main_event_loop` implements W3C SCXML Appendix D's two nested loops
# literally — the inner one runs eventless selection and the internal queue to
# quiescence, and neither loop asks whether the microstep moved the machine.
# Nothing in the code says that the second property is load-bearing, so the
# obvious "optimisation" is exactly the defect the other three engines shipped.
#
# Anchors are literal slices of the source; an edit that moves one is reported
# INCONCLUSIVE with the anchor quoted, never as a pass.

mutation_tests -p sce-rust-tests --test targetless_transition_completes_macrostep
mutation_targets backends/rust/runtime/src/engine.rs
mutation_targets backends/rust/runtime/src/helpers/microstep.rs
mutation_oracles backends/rust/tests/tests/targetless_transition_completes_macrostep.rs

# ── The macrostep ends at the external event ───────────────────────
#
# The defect the other three engines shipped, expressed here: take the external
# event's microstep and hand the machine back. The chain that microstep enabled
# is never walked, and the fixture reads `chained == 0` with the machine
# running in the state the document names.

mutation_case "the macrostep ends at the external event that opened it" <<'PY'
edit("backends/rust/runtime/src/engine.rs",
     """            if !self.process_next_external_event() {
                break;
            }
        }
    }""",
     """            let _ = self.process_next_external_event();
            break;
        }
    }""")
PY

# ── The internal queue is not the eventless queue ──────────────────
#
# Appendix D's inner loop drains BOTH, alternating: an eventless transition can
# raise, and what it raises can enable another eventless transition. Draining
# only the internal queue leaves the chain unwalked; draining only the
# eventless side leaves the raise queued. This mutation is the first of those,
# and the fixture's `arm` outcome is what sees it.

mutation_case "the inner loop drains the internal queue and skips eventless selection" <<'PY'
edit("backends/rust/runtime/src/engine.rs",
     """            let enabled = self.select_transitions(P::null_event());
            if !enabled.is_empty() {""",
     """            let enabled: TransitionSet<P::State, P::History> = TransitionSet::new();
            if !enabled.is_empty() {""")
PY

# The other half: the eventless side runs and the queue is left alone. The
# `<raise>` a targetless transition queued is never taken — and the outer loop,
# which will not take an external event while an internal one is queued, then
# turns forever, so the round's artefact timeout is what reports it.

mutation_case "the inner loop runs eventless selection and skips the internal queue" <<'PY'
edit("backends/rust/runtime/src/engine.rs",
     """            if !self.internal_queue.has_events() {
                // The queue emptied, so the chain — refused or merely finished —""",
     """            if true {
                // The queue emptied, so the chain — refused or merely finished —""")
PY

# ── The transition that moves nothing still runs ───────────────────
#
# The control's half. A targetless transition whose content never runs looks
# from the configuration exactly like one the engine handled and like an event
# it discarded, which is why the fixture counts `quiet` at all. The microstep
# is the runtime's transcription now, and it gives a targetless transition no
# branch of its own; the one way left to skip its content is to single it out
# where content is run.

mutation_case "a targetless transition runs none of its content" <<'PY'
edit("backends/rust/runtime/src/helpers/microstep.rs",
     """        if transition.has_actions {
            run.execute_transition_content(transition);
        }""",
     """        if transition.has_actions && !transition.is_targetless() {
            run.execute_transition_content(transition);
        }""")
PY
